        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(line): document threadBindings config and responsePrefix",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/line/src/config-schema.ts` defines `ThreadBindingsSchema` (5 active sub-fields + 2 deprecated aliases for session binding lifecycle) and `responsePrefix`, but `docs/channels/line.md` does not document the `threadBindings` config object or the `responsePrefix` field. Users configuring LINE cannot discover these features from the docs.\n\n- Problem: The `threadBindings` config object and `responsePrefix` exist in the LINE config schema/types but are absent from the docs\n- Solution: Add a \"Thread bindings\" section with config example and field descriptions (matching the Discord docs pattern), plus a `responsePrefix` mention in the Message behavior section\n- What changed: `docs/channels/line.md` (+33 lines — new H2 section + 1 line in Message behavior), `docs/docs_map.md` (+1 line for new heading)\n- What did NOT change: No code or behavior changes. Documentation only.\n\n**Missing fields**:\n1. **`threadBindings`** — object controlling how LINE conversations bind to agent sessions:\n   - `enabled` (boolean) — toggle thread bindings\n   - `idleHours` (number) — inactivity threshold before binding is considered idle\n   - `maxAgeHours` (number) — maximum binding lifetime; after expiry the binding is released and the next interaction follows the normal (unbound) flow\n   - `spawnSessions` (boolean) — gates explicit thread-bound spawn or bind operations (e.g. `sessions_spawn({ thread: true })` or ACP thread spawns). Does not automatically spawn a session on an ordinary first message. Default: `true`\n   - `defaultSpawnContext` (`\"fork\"` (default) | `\"isolated\"`) — session context mode\n   - `spawnSubagentSessions` / `spawnAcpSessions` — deprecated, migrated by `openclaw doctor --fix`\n2. **`responsePrefix`** (string) — prepended to every outbound reply\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Schema — `ThreadBindingsSchema` (`extensions/line/src/config-schema.ts:12-22`)\n\n```typescript\nconst ThreadBindingsSchema = z\n  .object({\n    enabled: z.boolean().optional(),\n    idleHours: z.number().optional(),\n    maxAgeHours: z.number().optional(),\n    spawnSessions: z.boolean().optional(),\n    defaultSpawnContext: z.enum([\"isolated\", \"fork\"]).optional(),\n    spawnSubagentSessions: z.boolean().optional(),\n    spawnAcpSessions: z.boolean().optional(),\n  })\n  .strict();\n```\n\n### Schema — `responsePrefix` via `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape` (`src/config/zod-schema.core.ts:657`)\n\n```typescript\nresponsePrefix: z.string().optional(),\n```\n\nThe LINE config schema extends `LineCommonConfigSchemaBase` which spreads `ReplyRuntimeConfigSchemaShape`, inheriting `responsePrefix` alongside other reply-formatting fields.\n\n### Runtime types (`extensions/line/src/types.ts:7-15,30,33`)\n\n```typescript\ninterface LineThreadBindingsConfig {\n  enabled?: boolean;\n  idleHours?: number;\n  maxAgeHours?: number;\n  spawnSessions?: boolean;\n  defaultSpawnContext?: \"isolated\" | \"fork\";\n  /** @deprecated Use spawnSessions instead. */\n  spawnSubagentSessions?: boolean;\n  /** @deprecated Use spawnSessions instead. */\n  spawnAcpSessions?: boolean;\n}\n\nresponsePrefix?: string;\nthreadBindings?: LineThreadBindingsConfig;\n```\n\nNote: `spawnSubagentSessions` and `spawnAcpSessions` are deprecated in favor of `spawnSessions`. The doc follows the Discord docs pattern — keeping them out of the normal example and noting deprecation in a separate line.\n\n### Runtime default — `defaultSpawnContext` (`src/channels/thread-bindings-policy.ts:212-216`)\n\n```typescript\nconst defaultSpawnContext =\n  normalizeSpawnContext(account?.defaultSpawnContext) ??\n  normalizeSpawnContext(root?.defaultSpawnContext) ??\n  normalizeSpawnContext(params.cfg.session?.threadBindings?.defaultSpawnContext) ??\n  \"fork\";  // ← runtime default\n```\n\n### Runtime — spawnSessions gating (`src/agents/subagent-spawn.ts:898`, `src/agents/acp-spawn.ts:706`)\n\n```typescript\nif (!policy.spawnEnabled) {  // spawnSessions controls this flag\n  // blocks subagent or ACP spawn\n}\n```\n\n`spawnSessions` gates explicit thread-bound subagent and ACP spawn operations, confirmed by `src/agents/tools/sessions-spawn-tool.ts:154` and `src/agents/runtime-capabilities.ts:60`. It does not automatically spawn sessions on ordinary first messages.\n\n### Test confirmation (`src/channels/thread-bindings-policy.test.ts:84`)\n\n```typescript\nexpect(policy.defaultSpawnContext).toBe(\"fork\");\n```\n\n### Sibling docs reference — Discord (`docs/channels/discord.md`)\n\n- `spawnSessions` controls auto-create/bind threads for `sessions_spawn({ thread: true })` and ACP thread spawns. Default: `true`.\n- `defaultSpawnContext` controls native subagent context for thread-bound spawns. Default: `\"fork\"`.\n- Deprecated `spawnSubagentSessions`/`spawnAcpSessions` keys are migrated by `openclaw doctor --fix`.\n- If thread bindings are disabled for an account, `/focus` and related thread binding operations are unavailable.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now discover the `threadBindings` config object and its 5 active sub-fields (plus 2 deprecated aliases) from the LINE channel docs, as well as the `responsePrefix` option. The documented `defaultSpawnContext` default (`\"fork\"`) matches the actual runtime behavior. These fields were already functional — they were simply invisible to users who configure via docs.\n",
